Logic change.
After RDRPcatch and Lucaprot, we do palmscan to both of them to there result, The RDRPcatch input for palmscan not change , but for lucaprot result ,input is :result/03_RDRP_identification/3_lucaprot/QutangGorge_M_7/RdRPs_only_using_threshold0.500000.csv
 the for mat of this  file protein_id,seq,prob,label
">lcl|ORF3_QutangGorge_M_7_0000000106:1301:234 unnamed protein product, partial",,0.9999157190322876,1


each RDRPcatch only have one rdrp region for one contig, but for lucaprot , it may have two region. separate them. Than check the region overlap between , if they overlap >over 50%, we think it same rdrp, otherwise , they are two different rdrp region on one contig, If they are same region, use RDRPcatch result as it RDRP_region. The RDRP region with overlap<50% would be lucaprot_only.


High-confidence_rdrp should be RdRpCATCH   palmscan   lucaprot  both yes, and same RDRP region, but if one rdrp in a contig in rdrp region is 3 yes , and it contain another rdrp only identified by lucaprot, this contig still High-confidence_RdRp






RdRpCATCH   palmscan   lucaprot   lucaprot_palmscan   → category
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
yes         yes        yes        *                   → High-confidence_RdRp
yes         yes        no         *                   → RDRPCatch_palmscan
yes         no         yes        *                   → RDRPCatch_lucaprot
yes         no         no         *                   → RDRPCatch_only
no          no         yes        yes (ABC motif)     → lucaprot_palmscan
no          no         yes        no  (no ABC motif)  → lucaprot_only
